# Copy to .env in this folder and edit; docker compose reads it automatically.
#
# Hosts OhmzBudget answers to (hostGuard), comma-separated, with or without
# port. localhost and 127.0.0.1 always work. When this is set, every other
# Host is refused with 403 — add the public hostname before exposing the
# stack through the tunnel. `ohmzbudget` is this compose service's own name:
# M2's container-to-container calls arrive with Host: ohmzbudget:3001, and
# hostGuard would 403 them without it:
# OHMZBUDGET_ALLOWED_HOSTS=localhost,127.0.0.1,ohmzbudget,budget.example.com
#
# Default when unset: localhost,127.0.0.1
#
# Private-network hosts the server may call (internalFetch), comma-separated.
# Entries match the URL's host exactly, so a host that listens on a
# non-default port must be written with it: `paperless:8000` matches, a bare
# `paperless` does not, and a `paperless:443` entry never matches an HTTPS
# target. Unused
# until M2's document bridge calls the paperless sidecar:
# OHMZBUDGET_INTERNAL_FETCH_ALLOW=paperless:8000
#
# Default when unset: empty (no private host is reachable)
